  "_comment": "Spell catalog (real data drives the schema). A Spell describes a castable action — what it does, who can cast it, what it costs. Spells that produce a lingering status reference an Effect by id under action_params.effect_id and supply the application-time params (save DCs, magnitudes that override the Effect's defaults) in action_params. Spells that produce one-shot results (damage, heal, teleport, summon) carry their action-specific data in action_params directly. The `action` field is the discriminator: damage, heal, apply_effect, cure_effect, teleport, summon, aoe_damage, turn_undead, knock, restore. See docs/data_dictionary/spell.md.",
